# The Vercel deploy is the STATIC SITE only (index + legal/marketing pages + assets).
# Everything below is app code, build artifacts, docs, or scratch — never web content.
# Keeps `vercel --prod` uploads small and prevents publishing non-site files.

# App + agent + server source (the API lives on Cloud Run, not Vercel)
StoreApp/
ProntoAgent/
CustodianPrototype/
pronto-server-cloudrun.mjs
package.json
package-lock.json

# Pod / engineering / docs / logs (not web content)
pod/
tests/
docs/
logs/
archive/

# Large local caches, build outputs & tooling (never upload)
.hf-cache/
.claude/
.vercel/
node_modules/
__pycache__/
release-candidates/
.playwright-cli/
StoreApp/AppPackages/

# Scratch / proof / prototype files — never publish
scratch_*.html
landing-*.png
*.py
*.ps1
*.bat
*.sh
*.md

# Kept (do NOT ignore): *.html at root, logo.png, assets/  — the served site.
